    "narrative": "As the Austin Waves navigate today\u2019s slate, offensive opportunities are constrained by a difficult matchup against Misiorowski, whose 2.35 xERA severely dampens the scoring floor for our active lineup. **Kyle Tucker** (47.99) remains our strongest play despite being relegated to the #8 spot in the order, which acts as a drag on his raw projection. His elite skill set keeps him in the marginal start category, though his output is clearly hindered by the SP skill disadvantage. Similarly, **Andy Pages** (42.38) barely clears our threshold for inclusion; while his platoon neutrality against the right-handed Misiorowski prevents a deeper collapse in his efficiency score, the combination of a tough opposing arm and a #7 lineup position limits his ceiling to a strictly volume-based play.\n\nOur bench strategy today is dictated by a lack of available games for key offensive contributors, as **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill** are all off today. The roster remains hampered by the absence of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who continues to reside on the IL, leaving our secondary depth\u2014including **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Franklin Arias**\u2014without an avenue for points today. With no viable alternatives to cycle in, we are forced to accept these lower-efficiency scores from **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** while prioritizing game participation to maintain our category volume, fully aware that Misiorowski\u2019s elite profile creates a significant risk of empty at-bats across the board.",
